// t_36492ad8 commit 1.  THE MIRROR OF fp_reach_unreached_undecl_id_f, and
// together they are the row for the SECOND mechanism this commit adds.
//
// Deferring the SEMANTIC diagnostic was not enough on its own: the IR builder
// lowered every non-prototype function, so an undeclared identifier in an
// unreachable body came back as "IR generation error: Unknown identifier" from
// a function the reference never compiles.  Lowering now skips functions the
// entry cannot reach.
//
// Unreachable, this exact body must compile CLEAN; reachable, as here, it must
// refuse.  One of the pair without the other proves nothing: suppressing the
// class everywhere satisfies the first, and lowering everything satisfies the
// second.
float4 unused(float4 t) { return t * zzz; }
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return unused(t); }
